==English==
{{swp|Extraction (military)}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|estraction}}, from {{der|en|ML.|extractio}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈstɹækʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extraction.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ækʃən|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An act of [[extracting]] or the condition of being [[extracted]].
# Something extracted, an [[extract]], as from a [[plant]] or an organ of an animal etc.
#* {{RQ:Milton Areopagitica|passage=They [books] do preserve as in a vial the purest efficacy and '''extraction''' of that living intellect that bred them.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A person's [[origin]] or [[ancestry]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Larissa Remennick|title=Russian Israelis: Social Mobility, Politics and Culture|publisher=Routledge|isbn=9781317977698|page=144
|passage=Our companion on these tours was a young tourist, an American of Russian '''extraction''', whose questions and remarks drew our attention to some details of Haifa life that have become too familiar and would have otherwise passed unnoticed.&nbsp;...}}
# {{lb|en|military}} An act of removing someone from a hostile area to a secure location.
# {{lb|en|dentistry}} A removal of a [[tooth]] from its [[socket]].

